@FEAT-003
Feature: Cart management # validation/features/cart_management.feature:2
  As a customer
  I want to add, remove, and adjust items in my cart
  So that I can manage my order before checkout
  @TC-009 @US-005 @positive @high
  Scenario: Add a dish to the cart                         # validation/features/cart_management.feature:8
    Given the meal "Salmon Roll" is available              # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:18
    When the customer taps "Add to cart" on "Salmon Roll"  # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:18
    Then "Salmon Roll" appears in the cart with quantity 1 # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:61
    And the cart total is updated "10.00" to include it    # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:66

  @TC-010 @US-005 @negative @high
  Scenario: Attempt to add an unavailable item                       # validation/features/cart_management.feature:15
    Given the meal "Salmon Roll" is marked unavailable               # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:45
    When the customer attempts to add "Salmon Roll" to the cart      # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:53
    Then the item is not added to the cart                           # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:72
    And the customer sees a message that it is currently unavailable # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:77

  @TC-011 @US-007 @positive @medium
  Scenario: Increase and decrease item quantity                        # validation/features/cart_management.feature:22
    Given "Salmon Roll" is already in the cart with quantity 1         # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:82
    When the customer increases the quantity by 2                      # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:92
    And the customer decreases the quantity by 1                       # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:100
    Then the cart shows "Salmon Roll" with quantity 2                  # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:108
    And the cart total is recalculated automatically after each change # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:113

  @TC-012 @US-006 @edge @medium
  Scenario: Decrease quantity to zero removes the item               # validation/features/cart_management.feature:30
    Given "Salmon Roll" is the only item in the cart with quantity 1 # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:121
    When the customer decreases the quantity to 0                    # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:126
    Then "Salmon Roll" is removed from the cart entirely             # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:131
    And the cart total updates to zero                               # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:136

  @TC-013 @US-005 @positive @high
  Scenario: Cart persists after a page reload                               # validation/features/cart_management.feature:37
    Given the customer has added an item to the cart in the current session # validation/features/steps/feature_steps.py:27
    When the customer reloads the page                                      # validation/features/steps/feature_steps.py:36
    Then the cart still shows the same items and quantities                 # validation/features/steps/feature_steps.py:45

  @TC-014 @negative @high
  Scenario: Reject an item from a different restaurant without changing the cart  # validation/features/cart_management.feature:43
    Given the cart contains an item from "Sushi Place"                            # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:141
    When the customer attempts to add an item from "Pizza Corner"                 # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:150
    Then the app blocks the action                                                # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:161
    And the existing cart remains unchanged                                       # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:167

@FEAT-004
Feature: Checkout # validation/features/checkout.feature:2
  As a customer
  I want to review my order and enter delivery details
  So that I can confirm my order before paying
  @TC-015 @positive @high
  Scenario: Proceed to checkout with a valid cart           # validation/features/checkout.feature:8
    Given the cart contains at least 1 available item       # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:233
    When the customer taps "Checkout"                       # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:242
    Then the order summary shows an itemized list           # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:247
    And the subtotal, delivery fee, and total are displayed # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:253

  @TC-016 @negative @medium
  Scenario: Checkout with an empty cart                         # validation/features/checkout.feature:15
    Given the cart is empty                                     # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:260
    When the customer navigates directly to the checkout screen # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:266
    Then checkout is rejected because the cart is empty         # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:274

  @TC-017 @positive @high
  Scenario: Enter a valid delivery address                # validation/features/checkout.feature:21
    Given the customer is on the checkout screen          # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:280
    When the customer enters a valid address and confirms # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:285
    Then the address is saved for this order              # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:291

  @TC-018 @negative @high
  Scenario: Enter an address outside the delivery zone  # validation/features/checkout.feature:27
    Given the restaurant's delivery radius is 5km       # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:296
    When the customer enters an address 10km away       # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:303
    Then checkout is blocked                            # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:317
    And the message "Outside delivery area" is shown    # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:322

  @TC-019 @edge @high
  Scenario: Item becomes unavailable mid-checkout                      # validation/features/checkout.feature:34
    Given the customer has reached the checkout screen                 # validation/features/steps/feature_steps.py:52
    When an item in the cart is marked unavailable by the backend      # validation/features/steps/feature_steps.py:58
    And the customer attempts to confirm the order                     # validation/features/steps/feature_steps.py:63
    Then the customer is notified before payment                       # validation/features/steps/feature_steps.py:73
    And the customer must remove or replace the item before proceeding # validation/features/steps/feature_steps.py:80

@FEAT-007
Feature: Delivery tracking # validation/features/delivery_tracking.feature:2
  As a customer
  I want to track my order
  So that I know when it will arrive
  @TC-028 @positive @high
  Scenario: Retrieve the order status sequence                                    # validation/features/delivery_tracking.feature:8
    Given the order has been confirmed and accepted by the restaurant             # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:446
    When the customer opens "Track order"                                         # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:451
    Then the status progresses through Preparing, Out for delivery, and Delivered # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:456

  @TC-029 @positive @medium
  Scenario: Track an order after an app restart                   # validation/features/delivery_tracking.feature:14
    Given an active order exists for the customer                 # validation/features/steps/feature_steps.py:194
    When the customer closes and reopens the app                  # validation/features/steps/feature_steps.py:200
    Then the tracking screen reloads the current status correctly # validation/features/steps/feature_steps.py:207
    And the status is not a stale or cached value                 # validation/features/steps/feature_steps.py:216

  @TC-030 @edge @low
  Scenario: Tracking when courier location is temporarily unavailable  # validation/features/delivery_tracking.feature:21
    Given the courier's GPS signal is lost temporarily                 # validation/features/steps/feature_steps.py:223
    When the customer views the tracking screen                        # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:471
    Then the app shows the last known location with a timestamp        # validation/features/steps/feature_steps.py:229
    And the map does not break or the app does not crash               # validation/features/steps/feature_steps.py:238

  @TC-031 @negative @medium
  Scenario: Order marked delivered without being tracked live  # validation/features/delivery_tracking.feature:28
    Given the backend marks the order as "delivered" directly  # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:465
    When the customer views the tracking screen                # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:471
    Then the current order status is "Delivered"               # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:477

@FEAT-002
Feature: Menu browsing # validation/features/menu_browsing.feature:2
  As a customer
  I want to view a restaurant's menu
  So that I can select food to order
  @TC-005 @positive @high
  Scenario: View full menu for a restaurant                                # validation/features/menu_browsing.feature:8
    Given the restaurant "Sushi Place" has an active menu with categories  # validation/features/steps/feature_steps.py:86
    When the customer selects "Sushi Place" from the results               # validation/features/steps/feature_steps.py:93
    Then the menu loads showing categories, item names, prices, and images # validation/features/steps/feature_steps.py:99

  @TC-006 @edge @medium
  Scenario: View menu for a currently closed restaurant  # validation/features/menu_browsing.feature:14
    Given a restaurant is outside its operating hours    # validation/features/steps/feature_steps.py:109
    When the customer selects that restaurant            # validation/features/steps/feature_steps.py:115
    Then the menu is viewable in browse-only mode        # validation/features/steps/feature_steps.py:121
    And items are marked unavailable                     # validation/features/steps/feature_steps.py:127
    And "Add to cart" is not allowed on any item         # validation/features/steps/feature_steps.py:132

  @TC-007 @negative @high
  Scenario: Menu fails to load due to a backend timeout          # validation/features/menu_browsing.feature:22
    Given the menu service is unreachable                        # validation/features/steps/feature_steps.py:144
    When the customer selects a restaurant                       # validation/features/steps/feature_steps.py:149
    Then the app shows a clear error message with a retry option # validation/features/steps/feature_steps.py:160
    And the app does not hang indefinitely                       # validation/features/steps/feature_steps.py:166

  @TC-008 @positive @low
  Scenario: View item details with allergen info            # validation/features/menu_browsing.feature:29
    Given the item "Salmon Roll" has allergen metadata set  # validation/features/steps/feature_steps.py:171
    When the customer taps on "Salmon Roll"                 # validation/features/steps/feature_steps.py:178
    Then the detail view shows the description and price    # validation/features/steps/feature_steps.py:183
    And allergen tags such as "contains fish" are displayed # validation/features/steps/feature_steps.py:189

@FEAT-006
Feature: Order confirmation # validation/features/order_confirmation.feature:2
  As a customer
  I want to receive confirmation of my order
  So that I know my order was accepted
  @TC-025 @positive @high
  Scenario: Confirmation shown after successful payment                 # validation/features/order_confirmation.feature:8
    Given the customer's payment has just succeeded                     # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:423
    When the customer views the post-payment screen                     # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:429
    Then a confirmation screen shows the order number, items, and total # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:434
    And an estimated delivery time is displayed                         # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:441

  @TC-026 @positive @medium
  Scenario: Confirmation notification is sent                            # validation/features/order_confirmation.feature:15
    Given the order has been successfully placed                         # validation/features/steps/feature_steps.py:244
    When up to 2 minutes have passed                                     # validation/features/steps/feature_steps.py:249
    Then the customer receives a confirmation email or push notification # validation/features/steps/feature_steps.py:254

  @TC-027 @edge @medium
  Scenario: Restaurant does not acknowledge the order in time             # validation/features/order_confirmation.feature:21
    Given the restaurant has not accepted the order within the SLA window # validation/features/steps/feature_steps.py:259
    When the SLA window elapses                                           # validation/features/steps/feature_steps.py:265
    Then the customer is notified of the delay                            # validation/features/steps/feature_steps.py:270
    And a support or cancellation option is surfaced                      # validation/features/steps/feature_steps.py:275

@FEAT-005
Feature: Payment # validation/features/payment.feature:2
  As a customer
  I want to pay for my order
  So that I can complete my purchase
  @TC-020 @positive @high
  Scenario: Pay successfully with a valid card                              # validation/features/payment.feature:8
    Given the customer has entered valid card details with sufficient funds # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:327
    When the customer submits the payment                                   # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:339
    Then the payment is authorized                                          # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:346
    And the order moves to the "confirmed" state                            # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:351

  @TC-021 @negative @high
  Scenario: Payment declined due to insufficient funds     # validation/features/payment.feature:15
    Given the customer's card has insufficient funds       # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:333
    When the customer submits the payment                  # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:339
    Then the order is not created                          # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:356
    And the customer sees the decline reason               # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:362
    And the customer can retry with another payment method # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:367

  @TC-022 @negative @high
  Scenario: Payment gateway timeout                                          # validation/features/payment.feature:23
    Given the payment provider is simulating a timeout                       # validation/features/steps/feature_steps.py:280
    When the customer submits the payment                                    # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:339
    Then the system does not double-charge the customer on retry             # validation/features/steps/feature_steps.py:289
    And the customer sees a "checking payment status" message until resolved # validation/features/steps/feature_steps.py:299

  @TC-023 @negative @medium
  Scenario: Invalid card number is rejected by the payment service  # validation/features/payment.feature:30
    When the customer enters a malformed card number                # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:373
    And the customer submits the payment form                       # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:379
    Then the payment is rejected with an invalid-card status        # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:384
    And the order remains unconfirmed                               # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:390

  @TC-024 @edge @high
  Scenario: Duplicate submission from double-clicking Pay                  # validation/features/payment.feature:37
    Given the customer is on the payment screen with valid details entered # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:396
    When the customer clicks "Pay" twice in quick succession               # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:401
    Then only one charge is created                                        # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:411
    And the second click is debounced or ignored                           # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:418

@FEAT-001
Feature: Restaurant discovery # validation/features/restaurant_discovery.feature:2
  As a customer
  I want to search for nearby restaurants
  So that I can choose where to order from
  @FEAT-001
  Feature: Restaurant discovery  # validation/features/restaurant_discovery.feature:2

  @TC-001 @positive @high
  Scenario: Search returns nearby restaurants                       # validation/features/restaurant_discovery.feature:11
    Given the customer has opened the app                           # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:40
    Given the customer has granted location permissions             # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:172
    And the demo restaurants are available                          # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:177
    When the customer performs a search with the default location   # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:182
    Then the results list shows restaurants sorted by distance      # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:187
    And each result has a name, rating, and estimated delivery time # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:193

  @TC-002 @edge @medium
  Scenario: Search with no results nearby                              # validation/features/restaurant_discovery.feature:19
    Given the customer has opened the app                              # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:40
    Given no restaurants are within 50km of the customer location      # validation/features/steps/feature_steps.py:304
    When the customer performs a search                                # validation/features/steps/feature_steps.py:310
    Then an empty-state message "No restaurants found nearby" is shown # validation/features/steps/feature_steps.py:315
    And no error or blank screen is displayed                          # validation/features/steps/feature_steps.py:321

  @TC-003 @negative @high
  Scenario: Search with location services disabled                  # validation/features/restaurant_discovery.feature:26
    Given the customer has opened the app                           # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:40
    Given the customer has denied location permission               # validation/features/steps/feature_steps.py:326
    When the customer attempts a search                             # validation/features/steps/feature_steps.py:331
    Then the app prompts for a manual address or to enable location # validation/features/steps/feature_steps.py:339
    And the app does not crash                                      # validation/features/steps/feature_steps.py:344

  @TC-004 @positive @medium
  Scenario: Filter restaurants by cuisine type            # validation/features/restaurant_discovery.feature:33
    Given the customer has opened the app                 # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:40
    Given search results include at least 2 cuisine types # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:204
    When the customer applies the "Italian" filter        # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:210
    Then only restaurants tagged "Italian" are shown      # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:215
    When the customer clears the filter                   # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:223
    Then all restaurants are shown again                  # validation/features/steps/application_steps.py:228

